au14-mast-untrained = You have no idea what to do with this. Mast work is an engineer's job.
au14-mast-examine-untrained = [color=gray]You would need engineering training to work on this.[/color]

au14-mast-examine-unkeyed = [color=yellow]No COMSEC keys are loaded. It relays nothing.[/color]
au14-mast-examine-keyed = Keyed for: [color=cyan]{ $factions }[/color].
au14-mast-examine-feed-open = [color=orange]The feed panel is open.[/color] A COMSEC fill card loads a key, a multitool wipes them all. Screw and weld it shut to put it on the air.

au14-mast-condition-keyed = Load at least one COMSEC key before sealing the feed.
au14-mast-condition-keyed-guide = Load a COMSEC fill card into the feed

au14-mast-key-blank = That card has no key this mast can use.
au14-mast-key-already = The mast already carries the { $faction } key.
au14-mast-key-start = You start loading the key into the feed...
au14-mast-key-done = { $faction } key loaded.
au14-mast-zeroize-empty = There are no keys in the feed to wipe.
au14-mast-zeroize-start = You start wiping the keys out of the feed...
au14-mast-zeroize-done = Every key is wiped. The mast is blank.

au14-mast-site-underground = A mast needs open sky. There is too much rock overhead down here.
au14-mast-site-roofed = A mast needs open sky - it cannot go up under a roof. You take the footing back up.
au14-mast-site-no-ground = There is no ground here to stake a footing into.
au14-mast-site-cramped = There is no room for the guy lines. A mast needs the tiles around it clear of walls.
au14-mast-site-crowded = Another mast or comms array stands too close. Masts this close would only drown each other out.
